---
import Guide from "../../../layouts/Guide.astro"
import Code from "../../../components/Code.astro"
import InstallCommand from "./partials/InstallCommand.astro"
import NextSteps from "./partials/NextSteps.astro"
import PickAndChoose from "./partials/PickAndChoose.astro"
import ServerSupport from "./partials/ServerSupport.astro"
---

<Guide overline="Guide">
  <Fragment slot="title">Getting started</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    OPUI ships first-class Svelte 5 components. Install the package, import what
    you need, and you're set.
  </Fragment>

  <section id="installation">
    <h2>Install via NPM</h2>
    <InstallCommand packages="svelte@5" />
  </section>

  <section id="css">
    <h2>Import the CSS</h2>
    <p>
      Svelte components ship markup only - the CSS still has to be imported
      once, in your root layout or the entry file that mounts your app. Import
      everything:
    </p>
    <Code
      code={`<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import "opui-css/css/imports.css"

  let { children } = $props()
</script>

{@render children()}`}
      lang="svelte"
    />
    <p>
      Or pick and choose in a CSS file, and import that file in your layout
      instead:
    </p>
    <PickAndChoose file="src/styles/main.css" />
    <Code
      code={`<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import "../styles/main.css"

  let { children } = $props()
</script>

{@render children()}`}
      lang="svelte"
    />
  </section>

  <section id="usage">
    <h2>How to use</h2>
    <Code
      code={`<script lang="ts">
  import { Button } from "opui-css/svelte"
</script>

<Button variant="filled">Click me</Button>`}
      lang="svelte"
    />
    <p>
      Containers take parts, such as <code>CardHeader</code> and
      <code>DialogFooter</code>. Other slots are snippets: the default slot is
      <code>children</code> and named slots are camelCased, such as
      <code>endText</code>. <code>TextField</code>, <code>Textarea</code>,
      <code>Select</code>, <code>Range</code>, <code>NumberField</code>,
      <code>OneTimeCode</code>, <code>Rating</code>, <code>Tabs</code> and
      <code>ToggleGroup</code> support <code>bind:value</code>.
      <code>Checkbox</code> and <code>Switch</code> support
      <code>bind:checked</code> and <code>bind:group</code>,
      <code>ToggleButton</code> supports <code>bind:checked</code>, and
      <code>Radio</code> supports <code>bind:group</code>.
    </p>
    <NextSteps />
  </section>

  <section id="ssr">
    <h2>Server rendering</h2>
    <p>
      Without hydration (SvelteKit with <code>csr = false</code>, or Astro with
      <code>@astrojs/svelte</code> and no <code>client:*</code> directive),
      every component renders complete HTML, and the native controls work and
      submit with their form. The props in the last column only update on the
      client, and the server icon next to each says what you see until then and
      how to work around it: a <code>bind:</code> value stays put while the
      native value still changes and submits. The table is read from the
      component sources and their API docs.
    </p>
    <ServerSupport framework="svelte" />
    <p>
      Hydrate those (<code>client:load</code> in Astro) or keep client-side
      rendering on. Component pages say what needs hydration next to the browser
      support chips, and the API tables mark each prop with a crossed-out server
      icon.
    </p>
  </section>
</Guide>
